  "descriptions": [
    {
      "description": "We establish the large scale convergence of a class of stochastic weakly nonlinear reaction-diffusion models on a three dimensional periodic domain to the dynamic $\\Phi^4_3$ model within the framework of paracontrolled distributions. Our work extends previous results of Hairer and Xu to nonlinearities with a finite amount of smoothness (in particular $C^9$ is enough). We use the Malliavin calculus to perform a partial chaos expansion of the stochastic terms and control their $L^p$ norms in terms of the graphs of the standard $\\Phi^4_3$ stochastic terms.",
      "descriptionType": "Abstract"
    }
  ],
